      "dom_id": "question-236454",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $5$ and the second term is $12.$\n\n$f(n)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,n\\ge 1$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are given the first term $f(1)=5.$ Also, the common difference of the sequence can be found as\n\n$$\nd=12-5=7.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =5+(n-1)(7) \\\\  & =5+7n-7 \\\\  & =7n-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
